# CI Triage needs no environment variables of its own.
#
# The model runs through the `claude` CLI on a Claude subscription. Locally, that is
# whatever `claude` is logged in as. In CI it will be a subscription token in a
# repository secret, generated with `claude setup-token`:
#
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
#
# MUST NOT BE SET, here or anywhere else on the machine. The billing guard refuses to
# run while any of these exist, whatever their value, because each one moves billing
# off the subscription. The full list is BILLING_ENV_VARS in
# triage/ci_triage/billing_guard.py; these are the common ones:
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN  ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL
#   CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK  CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX  CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY
#
# `npm run triage:doctor` checks this machine.
